Let $b$ and $y$ be the number of blue and yellow marbles, respectively. We are given that \begin{align*}
\frac{b}{y}&= \frac{4}{3} \quad \Longrightarrow \quad y = \frac{3}{4}b
\end{align*} After we add $5$ blue marbles and remove $3$ yellow marbles, we have \begin{align*}
\frac{b+5}{y-3}&= \frac{7}{3} \\
3(b+5) &= 7(y-3) \\
3b+15 &= 7y-21
\end{align*} Solving gives \begin{align*}
3b+15 &= 7(\frac{3}{4}b)-21 \\
3b+15 &= \frac{21}{4}b - 21 \\
9b &= 75 \\
b &= \boxed{25}
\end{align*}

